hadiths[23]{hadithnumber,text}:
"665","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah will say: O son of Adam! I asked you for food but you did not feed Me. He will say: O Lord! How could I feed You when You are the Lord of the worlds? He will say: Did you not know that My such-and-such servant asked you for food but you did not feed him? Did you not know that if you had fed him, you would have found (the reward of) that with Me. O son of Adam! I asked you for water but you did not give Me water to drink. He will say: O Lord! How could I give You water to drink when You are the Lord of the worlds? He will say: Did you not know that My such-and-such servant asked you for water, did you not know that if you had given him water to drink, you would have found (the reward of) that with Me? O son of Adam! I was ill but you did not visit Me. He will say: O Lord! How could I visit You when You are the Lord of the worlds? Allah, the Exalted, will say: Did you not know that My such-and-such servant was ill, if you had visited him, you would have found him with Me."" Or: ""You would have found Me with him."
"666","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith, and stated it in this way: ""If you had visited him, you would have found Me with him."
"667","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""In black seed there is a cure for every disease except as-sam, and as-sam is death."
"668","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Mushroom is a remnant of manna (the food that was sent down upon the Children of Israel), its water is a cure for the eye."
"669","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no reality in contagious disease, bad omen, and the misfortune of Safar."
"670","Abu’l-Hakam al-Bahili narrates: I went to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was having cupping done, so he said: Abu’l-Hakam! Have you ever had cupping done? He replied: I have never had cupping done. So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Abu’l-Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him) informed us that Jibril (peace be upon him) told him that among the things people use for treatment, cupping is the most beneficial."
"671","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says to fever: You are My fire; I impose you upon My believing servant in the world so that it may become his share from the fire of Hell."
"672","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever goes to a physiognomist or a soothsayer and affirms what he says (considers him truthful), then he has denied that which was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"673","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We (the companions of the Messenger) differed regarding the understanding of this verse: ""Like a bad tree, uprooted from the surface of the earth, having no stability."" We said: We think it is the mushroom. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came and said: ""What are you discussing?"" We said: About the tree mentioned by Allah in this verse. We said: We take it to mean the mushroom. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mushroom is from the « مَن » that was sent down upon the Children of Israel, its water is a cure for the eye, and the 'ajwah (date) is from Paradise and it is an antidote for poison."
"674","Sayyida Umm Akzar (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Let the bird remain in its nest (dwelling)."" (Do not make it fly for taking omens.)"
"675","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing those snakes that are found in houses, except for the snake with a cut tail and the one with two stripes, because both of them cause blindness and make women miscarry. So whoever leaves these two (without killing them) is not from among us."
"676","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The Ajwa dates of the upper region (Najd) are a cure, or they are an antidote for poison."
"677","Lady Umm Mundhir bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: One day, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to my house, and Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was with him. He had recovered from an illness and was therefore weak. There were bunches of half-ripe dates hanging in our house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) began to eat from them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Wait, you (have just recovered from illness and) are weak."" So Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) stopped. She (Umm Mundhir, may Allah be pleased with her) said: I had cooked barley and beetroot, then I brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ali! Take from this (and eat), for it is more beneficial for you."
"678","Narrated from Sayyida Umm Qais bint Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with her) that she brought her son to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I pressed his throat with my finger out of fear of a throat disease, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why do you press your children's throats with your finger like this? You should use this Indian wood (costus)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took her son, and he urinated on the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called for water and poured it over it or sprinkled it on it. The narrator said: Thus, this method became established that if a child does not eat food, water will be sprinkled on his urine, and if he eats food, his urine will be washed."
"679","Muhammad bin Hatib narrated: My mother took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). She had made broth, and it spilled on my body. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said something, but I did not know what it was. When the era of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) came, my mother told me: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had recited this supplication: ""Lord of the people! Remove the illness. You are the Healer. Grant healing. There is no healer except You."
"680","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had cupping done and gave the cupper his wage."
"681","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had cupping done and gave the cupper his wage."
"682","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had cupping done and medicine put into his nose."
"683","It is narrated from Abu Ja'far that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) applied oil medicine into his nose."
"684","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""O people! Seek treatment, for Allah has not created any disease except that He has also created its cure, except for «السام» , and «السام» means death."
"685","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Sharik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I was present when the Bedouins were asking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) questions: Is there any harm for us in doing such and such a thing? Is there any sin for us in doing such and such a thing? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! Allah has removed hardship/difficulty, except for the one who cuts off a portion from his brother’s honor; so this is the person who has sinned and is destroyed."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! Should we seek medical treatment? So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Seek medical treatment, for Allah has sent down a cure for every disease He has sent down, except death."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! What is the best thing that has been given to a servant? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Good character."
"686","Sayyiduna Usamah bin Shuraik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I was present with the Bedouins when they were asking questions to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then the narrator mentioned the same (incident), and in it, he narrated this addition: When they stood before him (the Prophet, peace be upon him), they began to kiss his blessed hand. The narrator said: I touched his blessed hand with mine, and it was more fragrant than musk."
"687","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If there is any good in the treatments you use, it is in the bloodletting done by the cupper."
